  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 17.33, p. 338. Book: EFL 100, BFL 63.95, NA -0.1875 (F/2.7), GIH 8.83 (HFOV=3.21), PTZ/F -24.49, VL 87.49, OD 296.43 (MAG -0.333). Wavelengths 0.541, 0.47, 0.57 um as in the book (primary first). Glass: LAFN2 entered as N-LAF2 (same nd and V as the book). The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 9, the rear of the cemented doublet, which reproduces the book's GIH (8.82 vs 8.83); the table has no plane stop row. The book designs this lens for 0.47 to 0.57 um and prints indices at 0.541 um (LAFN2 1.749, SF11 1.793, SK15 1.626). BFL here is the paraxial image distance for the finite object.",
